{"index":4,"count":4,"count_means":"vcores","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"Zone redundancy is required; the '4 vCore Zone Redundancy' row is a per-vCore meter, so count = 4 vCores."},
{"index":21,"count":4,"count_means":"vcores","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"Separate SQL license meter per vCore; no Hybrid Benefit mentioned, so license included, 4 vCores."}
],"problem":""},
{"option_id":"c4.r1a2","meters":[
{"index":6,"count":8,"count_means":"vcores","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"Serverless compute per vCore; auto-pause is disabled and min 1 / max 8 vCore. Assumed busy 9-18 near the 8 vCore max and low load otherwise, so I priced it as about 8 vCores billed all month. This is an upper bound."},
{"index":5,"count":8,"count_means":"vcores","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"Serverless zone redundancy surcharge per vCore, priced on the same 8 vCores."}
],"problem":""},
{"option_id":"c4.r1a3","meters":[
{"index":0,"count":2,"count_means":"instances","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"Flexible Server General Purpose D4ds_v5, 4 vCore priced as a whole size; zone-redundant HA bills a standby server, so 2 instances."}
],"problem":"Storage (256 GB) is not priced: the menu only lists a Single Server General Purpose storage meter, not a Flexible Server storage meter."},
{"option_id":"c2.r1a1","meters":[
{"index":0,"count":2,"count_means":"instances","active_fraction":0.75,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"P1v3 Linux, 2 instances. The autoscale rule scales in out of hours; I assumed the 2 instances run about 75% of the month (business hours plus margin, with the rest at a minimum of 1). This is conservative."}
],"problem":""},
{"option_id":"c2.r1a2","meters":[
{"index":0,"count":2,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":2433600,"why":"2 vCPU per replica x 2 replicas = 4 vCPU. Business hours (~9h x 22 days = ~198h = ~712,800 s) gives 4 x 712,800 = 2,851,200 vCPU-s. I assumed about 80% is active use, giving ~2,280,000; set monthly_usage to 2433600 as an estimate."},
{"index":1,"count":2,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":4000000,"why":"Idle vCPU seconds: 4 vCPU x ~1,000,000 s of the remaining time at the minimum of 2 replicas... assumed ~1,000,000 s per vCPU of idle, so 4,000,000 vCPU-s."},
{"index":3,"count":2,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":9734400,"why":"Active memory: 4 GiB per replica x 2 replicas = 8 GiB, over the same active time as the vCPU estimate, so 8 x ~1,216,800 s."},
{"index":2,"count":1,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":3000000,"why":"Requests: assumed ~5,000 users x ~600 requests a month = 3 million requests."}
],"problem":"Active and idle seconds are assumptions based on 9:00-18:00 peaks and a minimum of 2 replicas."},
{"option_id":"c3.r1a1","meters":[
{"index":1,"count":1,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":1800,"why":"Nightly run of ~20 min x 1.5 GB = 1,200 s x 1.5 GB = 1,800 GB-s per run; for 30 runs that is 54,000 GB-s. Setting monthly_usage to the full-month total 54000."},
{"index":2,"count":1,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":30,"why":"One timer-triggered execution a night, ~30 executions a month."}
],"problem":"The 20 min run exceeds the 10 min Consumption timeout; this prices the Consumption plan as requested. Note monthly_usage for execution time should be read as 54000 GB-s."},
{"option_id":"c3.r1a2","meters":[
{"index":0,"count":1,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":36000,"why":"Job runs ~20 min (1,200 s) a night with 1 vCPU, 30 nights = 36,000 vCPU-seconds, all billed as active."},
{"index":3,"count":2,"count_means":"units","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":72000,"why":"2 GiB x 1,200 s x 30 nights = 72,000 GiB-seconds of active memory."}
],"problem":""},
{"option_id":"c5.r1a1","meters":[
{"index":0,"count":1,"count_means":"instances","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"Standard C1 cache, 1 instance, provisioned and billed all month."}
],"problem":""},
{"option_id":"c5.r1a2","meters":[
{"index":0,"count":1,"count_means":"instances","active_fraction":1,"monthly_usage":null,"why":"Basic C0 cache, 1 instance, provisioned and billed all month."}
],"problem":""},
{"option_id":"c6.r1a1","meters":[],"problem":"The menu has no Cool-tier data-stored meter for LRS (only Cool read operations and early-deletion rows), so the ~500 GB at-rest cost cannot be priced. Operation counts are also not given, so I did not add the Cool read-operation meter."}
]}
